    detail:
      "Nothing reads web_vital: no check, no view, zero consumers against 2,073,919 analytics rows \u2014 and Check #8 of the website bot's charter has always been LCP. Before building that gate, the operand was measured, and it is not trustworthy. LCP is reported against navigation start, so a tab opened in the background does not paint until the visitor finally looks at it and the browser reports an honest LCP of however long that took. Across the 1,261 LCP rows written since the interaction-dedupe deployed, 74 (5.9%) exceed 60 seconds and the largest is 50,596 seconds. They are not inert: 162 rows are rated \u201cpoor\u201d and 74 of those 162 are poor ONLY because of this, so a speed gate built on today's data would have paged about pages that are fine. Fixed with the rule the web-vitals library uses \u2014 record the instant the page first became hidden and discard any LCP observed at or after it; a background tab is hidden from t=0, so all of its entries go. Three findings were refuted on the way rather than shipped: the apply-funnel check that had never once executed does work (verdict degraded, every field populated); its 9.3s cold read looked like a timeout risk against bot_sql's 20s ceiling and the planner says 123ms, all buffer hits; and the 99.87% collapse in interaction events on 2026-09-05 was a runaway emitter being FIXED by a deploy that landed the same hour, not an instrument dying. /apply itself is fast \u2014 p50 1,078ms, p75 1,632ms \u2014 which removes page speed as the explanation for the halved apply conversion MP-538 is chasing. The matching INP guard was written, then REVERTED and its tests deleted: it would have bought a 0.34% cleanup (2 of 596 rows) by discarding every interaction a visitor makes after their first tab-switch, and the existing terminal-flush test caught it. Three mutation proofs, each asserted to have landed before its verdict was read. A pre-existing test leak was fixed at the class: vi.unstubAllGlobals() does not undo vi.spyOn, so one test's unrestored visibilityState mock was handing \u201chidden\u201d to every test after it \u2014 inert until this file started grading visibility, at which point it failed two MP-514 tests against correct code. MP-540.",
