    detail:
      "The premise handed forward was that /apply had no form-level instrumentation and that building it was the next job. Re-measured first, and it inverted: event_category='interaction' does not span 182 days, its first row is 2026-09-11 \u2014 MP-512's instrumentation already shipped four days ago, apply_step_blocked included. What it cannot see is the gap it never covered. Measured across the 48 sessions it has recorded: 41 never advanced a step, and they are two populations with opposite remedies that apply_start merges under one name. 27 left in under 15 seconds (p50 dwell 5.1s) and 24 have no web_vital.INP row at all \u2014 they landed and never touched the form, and no form change reaches those people. The other 17 DO have an INP row, so they demonstrably interacted, and 7 of them stayed over a minute. They engaged and left anyway. Exactly ONE apply_step_blocked fired across all 41, so they are not quitting at a validation error; they quit mid-form, where an event that only fires on a Next press cannot see them by construction. apply_start is also not a start \u2014 it fires on mount, so it counts the form being rendered. Fixed by emitting apply_field_first_input once per distinct field the user actually edits: the first one in a session separates engaged from bounced, the last one names the field they quit on, and the whole path is recorded rather than only its endpoint. Deliberately NOT a pagehide 'abandon' event \u2014 track.ts registers its flush handlers at app boot, so a listener added on Apply mount fires after the queue has already drained and its event would never be sent. The load-bearing line is the type === 'change' gate: Apply.tsx restores a saved application by calling setValue() per field and RHF pushes those through the same watch subscription, so without it a returning visitor would be reported as having just engaged with every field they filled in on a previous visit. Field NAMES only, never values, holding the constraint MP-512 set for invalid_fields \u2014 this table accepts anonymous inserts. Nine contract tests import the real tracker instead of restating it, and three mutation proofs each assert the mutation LANDED before its verdict is believed; one of them did not land on the first attempt and the harness caught it rather than reporting a vacuous pass. v_apply_field_dropoff reads the result as scalar subqueries returning exactly one row in every state, including an empty table, so blank can never read as green \u2014 verified live, where sessions_engaged: 0 is printed beside a readability field saying the emitter is not deployed yet and that this is NOT evidence of zero engagement. MP-539.",
