      "The header band on every operating route is 37% shorter on desktop (140px → 88px) and 32% shorter on a phone (196px → 133px). PageHeader renders on 30+ routes, so its height is the most leveraged spacing number in the product — that band was spending the first screen restating a page title you had just clicked, pushing the actual work below the fold. Measured in headless chromium at 390/768/1440/1920, not estimated.",
