    label:
      "wave-licensing-stage-canonical: the same person could carry four contradicting licensing truths depending on which admin page you opened. 95 applicants read license_status='licensed' while license_progress still said 'unlicensed' — and all 95 carried a real licensed_at, most of them dated BEFORE they applied, so these were state-verified licences on people who came to Apex already licensed. The worse half was the write path: marking someone Licensed in License Push called an RPC that wrote license_progress and nothing else, while the call queue behind that page filters on license_status. So the one action whose entire purpose is to retire someone from the queue could not retire them from the queue, and could not promote them into the Licensed Inbox that gets people contracted. One person was sitting in exactly that state. Reconciliation now lives on the applications table itself, not in the RPC, because license_status is also written by the Xcel importer, the Apply form and three admin surfaces — patching one caller would have left the other four free to re-diverge. 109 drifting rows reconciled to 0, snapshotted first.",
