    label: "website-integrity-bot wave-28: stale-key-in-list guard installed as pre-commit hook (baseline ratchet at 165). Class-of-fix Round 11 sibling to wave-16..wave-27. Failure pattern: a dev writes `{rows.map((row, i) => <Row key={i} data={row} />)}` where `rows` is a DB-fetched array that reorders, inserts, or deletes mid-session (leaderboards, applicant queue, chargeback rows, notification hub, activity feed). React uses `key` for reconciliation; `key={i}` on a re-sortable list binds row-local state (form input value, drawer open state, focused ring, animated transition, mounted component instance) to POSITION not ROW. When the list mutates around a stage change, poll refresh, or optimistic update, that state bleeds onto the wrong row — the row that USED to sit at that position. On Sam's daily driver (mobile Safari per user_brand_and_handles + WEBSITE-INTEGRITY-BOT prompt §7) that means typing into an applicant note gets attached to a different applicant when the queue re-orders after a stage change; on desktop it means a focused search input jumps to the wrong row when a realtime subscription reorders the list. Same silent-corruption class as the 465 fake-success InsuraCloud sync rows (memory: project_apex_2026_05_18_insuracloud_auth_dead) and the 198 zombie AgentLink rows (memory: project_apex_2026_05_20_agentlink_fake_success): the action LOOKED successful (input received text, drawer opened, dropdown selected) but was bound to the wrong record — silent data attribution corruption Sam has no way to see in the UI. Built scripts/check-stale-key-in-list.mjs (~260 LOC): walks src/**/*.{tsx,jsx} (443 files) via a state-machine string/comment mask (line + block comments, single/double/backtick strings with escape sequences, template-literal `${…}` interpolation as real code — same skipper as check-blocking-modal wave-23). Detection regex `key=\\{(i|idx|index|arrayIndex)\\}` catches bare identifier keys only — `key={row.id}` / `key={row.slug}` / `key={item.uuid}` (property access) do NOT match, `key={i + 1}` / `key={idx.toString()}` (composition or method call) do NOT match, and `key={someHash}` (any non-index-named identifier) does NOT match. Only the four canonical index-var names (i, idx, index, arrayIndex) that scream 'this is a positional index used as a stable key' get caught. Baseline-count ratchet shape identical to check-blocking-modal (wave-23) + check-empty-catch pre-wave-24: BASELINE constant declared in-file at 165 — the exact count of unmarked sites at wave-28 launch — count can only DROP (fix a site by swapping to `key={row.id}` or annotate with `stable-key-allow:<reason>` marker), never rise. Distribution at launch: AgentCommandDashboard (25 sites — Sam's daily driver dashboard, mostly skeleton loaders + Recharts Cell for palette rotation), BookReconciliation (9 sites), Finances (6 sites), page-loading-skeleton (5 sites — all legit static-array skeletons), AdminStrikes (5 sites — mix of skeleton loader + stat row), CompactLeaderboard + ClientPipeline + LeaderboardTabs + LeadsLanding + ReadyModeIntegration + landing tickers + admin dialogs = the remainder. Pay-down pattern (wave-29+): each pay-down wave refactors 5-15 sites, either (a) swapping to `key={row.id}` / `key={row.slug}` where a stable id exists in the underlying view (DB rows, leaderboard entries, applicant queue rows — the real leak), or (b) annotating with `stable-key-allow:<why-index-is-safe-here>` marker for legit static arrays (skeleton loaders using `[...Array(N)].map`, hard-coded Brand Bible feature lists, decorative dot-grids). Lower BASELINE by exactly the count paid down each commit. Registered as npm run check:stale-key-in-list, wired into husky pre-commit chain (fires on any src/*.tsx|jsx or the script itself, 80-150ms cost — state-machine mask + linear regex over 443 files), appended to verify:core CI chain after check:hex-in-jsx-style. Guard end-to-end verified: (i) clean tree → OK 443 files scanned, 165 unmarked (== baseline 165); (ii) fail-injection sanity — created src/components/admin/__inject_wave28_test.tsx with `items.map((x, i) => <span key={i}>{x}</span>)` → guard exit 1 with correct 166-count FAIL + `src/components/admin/__inject_wave28_test.tsx:3 [key={i}]` fingerprint (167 file scan, 166 unmarked); (iii) same injection with `// stable-key-allow:test-static-array` comment on line above → guard exit 0 (444 files, 165 unmarked — opt-out honored); (iv) restored (rm inject file) → guard exit 0. Twenty-eighth surface audit since wave-4; thirteenth consecutive class-of-fix compounding asset. The commit-time ratchet now covers 11 classes of leak that used to require hand-audit weeks apart: internal-nav reload-trap (wave-16) / external-link tabnabbing (wave-17) / raw-db-slug leak (wave-18+20) / console-in-prod (wave-19) / empty-catch @ 0 (wave-21+24) / debugger @ 0 (wave-22) / blocking-modal baseline (wave-23) / raw-SQL-in-JSX @ 0 (wave-25) / @ts-ignore @ 0 (wave-26) / hex-in-JSX-style per-area (wave-27) / stale-key-in-list baseline (wave-28).",
